.TH ORO-WINDOW 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:window \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:window'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Provides ApplicationWindow class and methods
.PP
Don't use this module directly, get instances of ApplicationWindow with `oro:application` methods like `getCurrentWindow`, `createWindow`, `getWindow`, and `getWindows`.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBApplicationWindow (extends EventTarget)\fR
Represents a window in the application
.TP
\fBid()\fR
The unique ID of this window.
.TP
\fBindex()\fR
Get the index of the window
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fInumber\fR the index of the window
.TP
\fBhotkey()\fR
Documented method exposed by this module.
.TP
\fBchannel()\fR
The broadcast channel for this window.
.TP
\fBsize()\fR
Get the size of the window
.TP
\fBposition()\fR
get the position of the window
.TP
\fBtitle()\fR
get the title of the window
.TP
\fBfollowSystemTheme()\fR
Indicates whether the window follows the host desktop theme.
.TP
\fBpreferDarkTheme()\fR
Indicates whether the window prefers a dark theme when not following the system theme.
.TP
\fBisDarkMode()\fR
Whether the window is currently in dark mode.
.TP
\fBappearance()\fR
Current appearance metadata for the window.
.TP
\fBtoken()\fR
Documented method exposed by this module.
.TP
\fBstatus()\fR
get the status of the window
.TP
\fBgetSize()\fR
Get the size of the window
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fI{ width: number, height: number }\fR the size of the window
.TP
\fBgetPosition()\fR
Get the position of the window
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fI{ x: number, y: number }\fR the position of the window
.TP
\fBgetTitle()\fR
Get the title of the window
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring\fR the title of the window
.TP
\fBgetStatus()\fR
Get the status of the window
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fInumber\fR the status of the window
.TP
\fBclose()\fR
Close the window Android rejects with `ENOTREADY` while Activity state is saved or unavailable.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<object>\fR the options of the window
.TP
\fBshow()\fR
Shows the window Android rejects with `ENOTREADY` while Activity state is saved or unavailable.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ipc.Result>\fR
.TP
\fBhide()\fR
Hides the window Android rejects with `ENOTREADY` while Activity state is saved or unavailable.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ipc.Result>\fR
.TP
\fBfocus()\fR
Brings the window to the foreground and focuses it.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ipc.Result>\fR
.TP
\fBblur()\fR
Removes focus from the window (desktop: sends to back; mobile: hides).
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ipc.Result>\fR
.TP
\fBmaximize()\fR
Maximize the window
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ipc.Result>\fR
.TP
\fBminimize()\fR
Minimize the window
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ipc.Result>\fR
.TP
\fBrestore()\fR
Restore the window
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ipc.Result>\fR
.TP
\fBsetTitle(title)\fR
Sets the title of the window
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fItitle\fR (string; required) the title of the window
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ipc.Result>\fR
.TP
\fBsetSize(opts)\fR
Sets the size of the window
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIopts\fR (object; required) an options object
.br
\fIopts.width\fR (number \\| string; optional) the width of the window
.br
\fIopts.height\fR (number \\| string; optional) the height of the window
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ipc.Result>\fR
.TP
\fBsetPosition(opts)\fR
Sets the position of the window
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIopts\fR (object; required) an options object
.br
\fIopts.x\fR (number \\| string; optional) the x position of the window
.br
\fIopts.y\fR (number \\| string; optional) the y position of the window
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<object>\fR
.TP
\fBnavigate(path)\fR
Navigate the window to a given path
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIpath\fR (object; required) file path
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ipc.Result>\fR
.TP
\fBshowInspector()\fR
Opens the Web Inspector for the window (desktop only).
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<object>\fR
.TP
\fBmarkReady()\fR
Acknowledges that this window has a usable application screen. Call after mounting the UI and loading required styles. Android apps configured with `[webview] require_ready = true` keep native startup recovery armed until this acknowledgement. Only the current window can acknowledge its own readiness. This does not replay operations or establish application authorization.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBmarkPresented()\fR
Reveals this Android window's verified bundled startup screen after a native visual\-state fence. Call after installing its inline styles and startup UI. This does not acknowledge application readiness or stop the 30\-second native watchdog. Keep application controls inert until the usable screen calls markReady(). Failed startup restores native recovery and its Reload control. Requires the current trusted top\-level document; foreign origins, headless windows and stale documents cannot reveal a startup screen. Other platforms reject with ENOSYS. Hidden windows do not gain focus from this call.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBsetBackgroundColor(opts)\fR
Sets the background color of the window
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIopts\fR (object; required) an options object
.br
\fIopts.red\fR (number; required) the red value
.br
\fIopts.green\fR (number; required) the green value
.br
\fIopts.blue\fR (number; required) the blue value
.br
\fIopts.alpha\fR (number; required) the alpha value
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<object>\fR
.TP
\fBgetBackgroundColor()\fR
Gets the background color of the window
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<string>\fR
.TP
\fBsetContextMenu(options)\fR
Opens a native context menu.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; required) an options object
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<object>\fR
.TP
\fBsetAlwaysOnTop(enabled)\fR
Sets whether the window should stay always on top (desktop only).
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIenabled\fR (boolean; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ipc.Result>\fR
.TP
\fBisAlwaysOnTop()\fR
Checks if the window is set to always be on top (desktop only).
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<boolean>\fR
.TP
\fBshowOpenFilePicker(options)\fR
Shows a native open file dialog.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; required) an options object
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<string[]>\fR an array of file paths
.TP
\fBshowSaveFilePicker(options)\fR
Shows a native save file dialog.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; required) an options object
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<string \\| null>\fR the selected file path or null
.TP
\fBshowDirectoryFilePicker(options)\fR
Shows a native directory dialog.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; required) an options object
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<string[]>\fR an array of file paths
.TP
\fBshare(options)\fR
Opens the platform share sheet for the current window. New Android file opens expire after 24 hours. Recipients can retain copies. Resolution means a share target was selected, not that delivery completed.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ShareOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBsetSystemAppearance(options)\fR
Sets Android 11+ system surfaces for this window. The foreground window owns appearance; `system` follows configuration changes. Insets/IME updates arrive as `windowinsetschange` CustomEvents. Earlier Android versions and other platforms reject with `ENOSYS`.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (SystemAppearanceOptions; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBsetFullscreen(enabled)\fR
Enters or exits Android 11+ native fullscreen for the current foreground window. First select explicit inset ownership with setSystemAppearance. A native Exit fullscreen control, Back, suspension, hiding, and renderer destruction exit presentation. Entry never captures a pointer or hides IME. Observe windowfullscreenchange for native exits. Browser DOM fullscreen is a separate capability. Other platforms reject with ENOSYS.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIenabled\fR (boolean; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<FullscreenState>\fR
.TP
\fBgetFullscreenState()\fR
Reads Android native fullscreen state for the current foreground window. Other platforms reject with ENOSYS.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<FullscreenState>\fR
.TP
\fBsetContentProtection(enabled)\fR
Requests Android FLAG_SECURE while this window is visible. The whole native activity is protected, including recents previews and ordinary screenshots. This does not protect clipboard, shared files, external displays, or secrets already exported by the application. Custom native flag owners must coordinate with this runtime API. Other platforms reject with ENOSYS.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIenabled\fR (boolean; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ContentProtectionState>\fR
.TP
\fBsend(options)\fR
This is a high\-level API that you should use instead of `ipc.request` when you want to send a message to another window or to the backend.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; required) an options object
.br
\fIoptions.window\fR (number; optional) the window to send the message to
.br
\fIoptions.backend\fR (boolean; optional; default false) whether to send the message to the backend
.br
\fIoptions.event\fR (string; required) the event to send
.br
\fIoptions.value\fR (string \\| object; optional) the value to send
.TP
\fBpostMessage(data)\fR
Post a message to a window TODO(@jwerle): research using `BroadcastChannel` instead
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIdata\fR (object; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise\fR
.TP
\fBopenExternal(value)\fR
Opens an URL in the default application associated with the URL protocol, such as 'https:' for the default web browser.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIvalue\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<{ url: string }>\fR
.TP
\fBrevealFile(value)\fR
Opens a file in the default file explorer.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIvalue\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise\fR
.TP
\fBupdate()\fR
Updates window state
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ipc.Result>\fR
.TP
\fBaddListener(event, cb)\fR
Adds a listener to the window.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIevent\fR (string; required) the event to listen to
.br
\fIcb\fR (function(*): void; required) the callback to call
.TP
\fBon(event, cb)\fR
Adds a listener to the window. An alias for `addListener`.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIevent\fR (string; required) the event to listen to
.br
\fIcb\fR (function(*): void; required) the callback to call
.TP
\fBonce(event, cb)\fR
Adds a listener to the window. The listener is removed after the first call.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIevent\fR (string; required) the event to listen to
.br
\fIcb\fR (function(*): void; required) the callback to call
.TP
\fBremoveListener(event, cb)\fR
Removes a listener from the window.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIevent\fR (string; required) the event to remove the listener from
.br
\fIcb\fR (function(*): void; required) the callback to remove
.TP
\fBremoveAllListeners(event)\fR
Removes all listeners from the window.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIevent\fR (string; required) the event to remove the listeners from
.TP
\fBoff(event, cb)\fR
Removes a listener from the window. An alias for `removeListener`.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIevent\fR (string; required) the event to remove the listener from
.br
\fIcb\fR (function(*): void; required) the callback to remove
